                "artifacts": [
                    {
                        "artifact_key": "get_imo_account",
                        "tablename": "get_imo_account",
                        "name": "IMO - Account ID",
                        "description": "Parses the local IMO account (account ID and name) from the IMO accountdb.db.",
                        "author": "@markmckinnon",
                        "created_date": "2021-03-11",
                        "last_updated_date": "2026-10-04",
                        "notes": "",
                        "category": "IMO"
                    },
                    {
                        "artifact_key": "get_imo_messages",
                        "tablename": "get_imo_messages",
                        "name": "IMO - Messages",
                        "description": "Parses IMO messages (timestamp, direction, chat partner, message, sender and recipient IDs, read status and attachment path) from the messages table of imofriends.db. Rows are read from the messages table alone, and the timestamp column is read as nanoseconds since 1970.",
                        "author": "@markmckinnon",
                        "created_date": "2021-03-11",
                        "last_updated_date": "2026-10-04",
                        "notes": "Direction is decoded from the messages table 'message_type' column. Direction is mapped from message_type values 1 Incoming and 2 Outgoing; that mapping is not sourced from the app. Unrecognized values are reported as stored, so rows the mapping does not cover are not labelled as sent or received.\nIn the conversation view only rows labelled Outgoing are attributed to the device owner; a row whose direction value is blank or unrecognized is not attributed to the owner.\nFrom ID and To ID are filled only when the direction is recognized; the other party is reported in Chat Partner regardless.\nOn pixel7a_a14 (22 rows) and pixel3_a12 (14 rows) message_type held only 0 and 1 (11 and 11, 8 and 6), so the rows holding 0 show 0 in Direction and no row was labelled Outgoing; what 0 means is not established.\nNo source for the unit of the timestamp column was found. Read as nanoseconds since 1970 its values fall on 2024-04-21 to 2024-04-22 on pixel7a_a14 and on 2021-11-23 to 2021-11-24 on pixel3_a12, and every stored value on both was a whole number of milliseconds. The Timestamp column is cut to whole seconds, and is blank when the stored value is empty.\nRows are read from the messages table alone, so a message whose buid has no row in the friends table is still reported; neither tested image held such a message. A query error is written to the run log.",
                        "category": "IMO"
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "module_name": "healthConnect",
                "module_filename": "healthConnect.py",
                "artifacts": [
                    {
                        "artifact_key": "healthconnect_apps",
                        "tablename": "healthconnect_apps",
                        "name": "Health Connect - Apps",
                        "description": "Apps registered with the Android Health Connect store, read from the application_info_table of healthconnect.db.",
                        "author": "@danjethh, Claude",
                        "created_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "last_updated_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "notes": "Health Connect is the Android framework store that apps write health and fitness records to and read them from; its SQLite database is healthconnect.db in system_ce/<user>/healthconnect. Package, App Name and the stored App Icon come from application_info_table. Record Types Used is the comma separated list of numeric record type ids the table holds; each id is shown with the name the AOSP RecordTypeIdentifier class gives it, and an id that class does not name is shown as stored. The column is empty where the table stores no value. Android User is the number in the system_ce path. A row here shows that the platform kept an entry for the package; it does not show that the app wrote or read any record, which the record artifacts and the access log artifacts show. Verified on Android 16 full file system extractions of two Samsung phones (Health Connect database schema versions 20 and 23), on which the table held two platform packages and no fitness app, and on two further Samsung phones (schema version 26), on which it held those two and a third row whose package name starts com.android.healthconnect.phone, again with no fitness app. On the corpus, kevin_pocox7_a15 (Android 15) and pixel7a_a14 (Android 14) gave 2 and 3 rows, equal to their application_info_table rows. On the contributor's four extractions Record Types Used was empty on every row and Android User held one value (0) on every row.",
                        "category": "Health Connect"
                    },
                    {
                        "artifact_key": "healthconnect_preferences",
                        "tablename": "healthconnect_preferences",
                        "name": "Health Connect - Preferences",
                        "description": "Key and value pairs of the preference_table of healthconnect.db.",
                        "author": "@danjethh, Claude",
                        "created_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "last_updated_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "notes": "Keys and values are reported as stored; the meaning of a key is not established here, and a key the store does not contain is not evidence about the setting it would hold. On the two Android 16 extractions tested first the table held seven keys (for example inactive_apps_added, migration_state, onboarding_state_0), one of them a UTC time written as text (current_state_start_time), which is shown as stored; on two further extractions (schema version 26) it held those seven and two more, app_icons_resize_completed_key and synthetic_package_name_salt. Android User is the number in the system_ce path. On the contributor's four extractions Android User held one value (0) on every row.",
                        "category": "Health Connect"
                    },
                    {
                        "artifact_key": "healthconnect_first_grants",
                        "tablename": "healthconnect_first_grants",
                        "name": "Health Connect - Permission First Grant Times",
                        "description": "Per package or shared-user entry times from health-permissions-first-grant-times.xml, which sits beside healthconnect.db.",
                        "author": "@danjethh, Claude",
                        "created_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "last_updated_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "notes": "Each package or shared-user element carries a name and a first-grant-time written as an ISO 8601 UTC string, which is shown as stored and also converted to a time; Entry Type says which element the row came from, and the Package column holds the name attribute of either. The file is read as plain XML or as Android binary XML, whichever it is. On the contributor's Android 16 extractions the file held package or shared-user elements, and what a shared-user name identifies is not established here; kevin_pocox7_a15 holds one of each in the same file. What the file records beyond its name is not established here: it is not evidence that the package wrote or read any health record. Android User is the number in the system_ce path.",
                        "category": "Health Connect"
                    },
                    {
                        "artifact_key": "healthconnect_activity",
                        "tablename": "healthconnect_activity",
                        "name": "Health Connect - Activity Records",
                        "description": "Interval records of the Health Connect store that carry one quantity over a start and end time: steps, distance, active and total energy, floors climbed, elevation gained, hydration and wheelchair pushes.",
                        "author": "@danjethh, Claude",
                        "created_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "last_updated_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "notes": "One row per record from steps_record_table, distance_record_table, active_calories_burned_record_table, total_calories_burned_record_table, floors_climbed_record_table, elevation_gained_record_table, hydration_record_table and wheelchair_pushes_record_table. Start and End are epoch milliseconds shown as UTC; the zone offsets are the seconds the writing app supplied and are shown as +HH:MM. Units follow the AOSP internal record classes: distance and elevation in metres, energy in calories (the unit of the AOSP Energy class, not kilocalories), hydration in litres; floors, steps and wheelchair pushes are counts. Package and App Name come from the record's app_info_id, Device Manufacturer, Model and Type from its device_info_id, and Recording Method is the number the record stores, shown with the Metadata.RECORDING_METHOD_* name. Last Modified is the time the store recorded for the row. Client Record ID is the identifier the writing app chose. Record UUID is the 16 byte uuid as hex. The values are what the writing app supplied; the store does not establish who or what produced them, so a manual entry or an app that imports from another source is a possibility the examiner has to rule out with Recording Method, the app and the device columns. Calories burned and distance totals may overlap between apps. Evidence tier: data-proven on two corpus stores, source-verified for the units. The table and column names were checked against the database schema of two Android 16 extractions and the units against the AOSP HealthFitness module (commit 45168a88ae2a7e1abafe1cc81001d97ff00194e2), and the output was exercised on a synthetic database of the same schema. On two corpus stores, kevin_pocox7_a15 (schema version 20) and pixel7a_a14 (schema version 12), the artifact reported 68,617 and 79,052 rows, equal to the rows of the tables it reads, and for every steps row the start time (to the second in LAVA, to the millisecond in the TSV) and the count equalled the values in the store; the contributor's four Android 16 extractions held no record. On both corpus stores Device Manufacturer and Device Model were empty on every row because device_info_table stores no manufacturer or model there. Speed records (speed_record_table, 1,784 rows on pixel7a_a14) and skin temperature records (skin_temperature_record_table, 65 rows, with 9 rows in skin_temperature_delta_table, on kevin_pocox7_a15) are not read by any Health Connect artifact. Reproductive health, medical record and other record tables are not read.",
                        "category": "Health Connect"
                    },
                    {
                        "artifact_key": "healthconnect_measurements",
                        "tablename": "healthconnect_measurements",
                        "name": "Health Connect - Measurements",
                        "description": "Single point in time records of the Health Connect store: weight, height, body composition, resting heart rate, oxygen saturation, respiratory rate, heart rate variability, VO2 max, blood pressure, blood glucose, body temperature and basal metabolic rate.",
                        "author": "@danjethh, Claude",
                        "created_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "last_updated_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "notes": "One row per record from the instant record tables: weight, height, body_fat, lean_body_mass, bone_mass, body_water_mass, resting_heart_rate, oxygen_saturation, respiratory_rate, heart_rate_variability_rmssd, vo2_max, blood_pressure, blood_glucose, body_temperature, basal_body_temperature and basal_metabolic_rate. Units follow the AOSP internal record classes: weight and body masses in grams, height in metres, percentages as a percent number, blood pressure in mmHg, blood glucose in mmol/L, temperature in degrees Celsius, basal metabolic rate in watts, heart rate variability in milliseconds, resting heart rate in beats per minute, VO2 max in mL/min/kg and respiratory rate in breaths per minute. Detail holds the enumerated fields of a record (measurement location, body position, meal relation, measurement method) as stored numbers; their names are not decoded here. Time is epoch milliseconds shown as UTC with the zone offset the writing app supplied. The other columns work as in the Activity Records artifact, and so does its caution about the origin of a value. Evidence tier: data-proven on two corpus stores: the artifact reported 535 rows on kevin_pocox7_a15 and 8 on pixel7a_a14, equal to the rows of the tables it reads; the contributor's Android 16 extractions held none. Reproductive health records are not read.",
                        "category": "Health Connect"
                    },
                    {
                        "artifact_key": "healthconnect_heart_rate",
                        "tablename": "healthconnect_heart_rate",
                        "name": "Health Connect - Heart Rate Samples",
                        "description": "Heart rate samples of the Health Connect store, each with the record that holds it.",
                        "author": "@danjethh, Claude",
                        "created_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "last_updated_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "notes": "heart_rate_record_series_table holds one row per sample (beats_per_minute and epoch_millis) and its parent_key names the row of heart_rate_record_table, which carries the record's start and end time, app, device and recording method. Sample Time is epoch milliseconds shown as UTC. The other columns work as in the Activity Records artifact. Evidence tier: data-proven: on kevin_pocox7_a15 and pixel7a_a14 the artifact reported 169,098 and 35,166 samples, and every sample's time (to the second in LAVA, to the millisecond in the TSV) and beats per minute equalled the stored series values; the contributor's Android 16 extractions held none. Resting heart rate records are in the Measurements artifact.",
                        "category": "Health Connect"
                    },
                    {
                        "artifact_key": "healthconnect_sleep",
                        "tablename": "healthconnect_sleep",
                        "name": "Health Connect - Sleep Sessions",
                        "description": "Sleep session records of the Health Connect store.",
                        "author": "@danjethh, Claude",
                        "created_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "last_updated_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "notes": "One row per row of sleep_session_record_table, with the title and notes the writing app supplied and the number of rows sleep_stages_table holds for the session (Stage Count). Start and End are epoch milliseconds shown as UTC with the zone offsets the writing app supplied. The other columns work as in the Activity Records artifact. A session is what the writing app reported; it does not establish that the person slept. Evidence tier: data-proven: 98 and 17 sessions on kevin_pocox7_a15 and pixel7a_a14, equal to the stored session rows; Title and Notes were empty on every row of both. The contributor's Android 16 extractions held none.",
                        "category": "Health Connect"
                    },
                    {
                        "artifact_key": "healthconnect_sleep_stages",
                        "tablename": "healthconnect_sleep_stages",
                        "name": "Health Connect - Sleep Stages",
                        "description": "Stage rows of sleep_stages_table with the session they belong to.",
                        "author": "@danjethh, Claude",
                        "created_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "last_updated_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "notes": "Stage Type is the number stored, shown with the SleepSessionRecord.StageType name of the AOSP framework (0 unknown, 1 awake, 2 sleeping, 3 awake out of bed, 4 light, 5 deep, 6 REM, 7 awake in bed); a number that class does not name is shown as stored. Stage times are epoch milliseconds shown as UTC. Session Start, Session End and the app columns come from the parent session row. Evidence tier: data-proven: 5,957 and 1,025 stage rows on kevin_pocox7_a15 and pixel7a_a14, and every stage's start time and type equalled the values in the store.",
                        "category": "Health Connect"
                    },
                    {
                        "artifact_key": "healthconnect_exercise",
                        "tablename": "healthconnect_exercise",
                        "name": "Health Connect - Exercise Sessions",
                        "description": "Exercise session records of the Health Connect store.",
                        "author": "@danjethh, Claude",
                        "created_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "last_updated_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "notes": "One row per row of exercise_session_record_table. Exercise Type is the number stored, shown with the name of the AOSP ExerciseSessionType class; a number that class does not name is shown as stored. Title and Notes are the text the writing app supplied. Has Route is Yes or No from the stored has_route flag, blank where it is null; Route Points, Lap Count and Segment Count are the number of rows the exercise_route_table, exercise_laps_table and exercise_segments_table hold for the session, and the route points themselves are in the Exercise Route artifact. Rate of Perceived Exertion is the stored session_rate_of_perceived_exertion where the column exists. The other columns work as in the Activity Records artifact. Evidence tier: data-proven: 126 and 16 sessions on kevin_pocox7_a15 and pixel7a_a14, equal to the stored session rows; Title and Notes were empty on every row of both.",
                        "category": "Health Connect"
                    },
                    {
                        "artifact_key": "healthconnect_access_logs",
                        "tablename": "healthconnect_access_logs",
                        "name": "Health Connect - Access Logs",
                        "description": "access_logs_table of the Health Connect store: which app read, wrote or deleted which record types, and when.",
                        "author": "@danjethh, Claude",
                        "created_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "last_updated_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "notes": "Access Time is epoch milliseconds shown as UTC. Operation is the stored operation_type shown with the name used by the AOSP Constants class (0 upsert, 1 delete, 2 read). Record Types is the comma separated list of numeric record type ids stored, each shown with the name of the AOSP RecordTypeIdentifier class. Medical Resource Type and Medical Data Source Accessed are shown as stored where the columns exist. The app is the row of application_info_table that app_id points to. A log row records an access the platform logged; the log's retention period is not established here, so the absence of a row is not evidence that no access took place. Evidence tier: data-proven: 2,972 and 855 rows on kevin_pocox7_a15 and pixel7a_a14, equal to the stored access_logs_table rows.",
                        "category": "Health Connect"
                    },
                    {
                        "artifact_key": "healthconnect_change_logs",
                        "tablename": "healthconnect_change_logs",
                        "name": "Health Connect - Change Logs",
                        "description": "change_logs_table of the Health Connect store: upserts and deletes the store logged per app and record type.",
                        "author": "@danjethh, Claude",
                        "created_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "last_updated_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "notes": "Record Type is the stored numeric id shown with the AOSP RecordTypeIdentifier name; Operation is shown with the name used by the AOSP Constants class (0 upsert, 1 delete). UUID Count is the number of 16 byte UUIDs the uuids blob holds and UUIDs lists them as hex. Time is epoch milliseconds shown as UTC. Medical Resource Type and Medical Data Source ID are shown as stored where the columns exist. The store trims this table, so the absence of a row is not evidence that no change took place. Evidence tier: data-proven: 9,957 and 3,472 rows on kevin_pocox7_a15 and pixel7a_a14, equal to the stored change_logs_table rows.",
                        "category": "Health Connect"
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "module_name": "siminfo",
