                        "created_date": "2023-02-24",
                        "last_updated_date": "2023-02-24",
                        "notes": "Parses the cached values in the com.facebook shared_prefs XML only. No online lookup is made. The last_refresh, data_access_expiration_time and expires_at values are converted to UTC, read as milliseconds when 13 digits long and as seconds otherwise.",
                        "category": "Garmin"
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "module_name": "androidauto",
                "module_filename": "androidauto.py",
                "artifacts": [
                    {
                        "artifact_key": "extract_android_auto",
                        "tablename": "extract_android_auto",
                        "name": "Android Auto - Allowed Cars",
                        "description": "Rows of the allowedcars table in Android Auto's carservicedata.db: car and head unit details, with the connectiontime column read as a Unix millisecond time",
                        "author": "its5Q, @AlexisBrignoni, Codex",
                        "created_date": "2025-07-28",
                        "last_updated_date": "2026-10-25",
                        "notes": "One row per row of the allowedcars table. On every copy examined the same database also has a rejectedcars table with the same columns; the Android Auto - Rejected Cars artifact reads it. Android Auto is closed source and what places a car in allowedcars, or what event the connectiontime column marks, is not established; a row is not by itself shown to be a completed connection. The connectiontime column is declared INTEGER and held a 13-digit value on all 15 rows found in 8 of the 11 corpus images that hold the database, and on all 8 rows of one further Android 16 image, read here as Unix milliseconds and shown in UTC to the second. Each carservicedata.db is read once per Android user; duplicate storage views of one copy are collapsed to one, and Source File names the copy a row came from.",
                        "category": "Android Auto"
                    }
