                        "notes": "Thanks to Josh Hickman for the research. An explicitly present value attribute is retained, including an empty attribute. Only when value is absent on an exact unnamespaced string element is its direct parsed child.text reported, or an empty string if that text is absent. Text is not stripped; ElementTree XML normalization and existing recovery apply. This does not retain nested text, tails, sets or original XML bytes, interpret preference meanings, or establish absence versus an explicit empty value. Existing file selection, source union and required name behavior are unchanged.",
